# GitHub's language bar counts raw bytes, and a saved .ipynb is mostly
# embedded output - rendered tables and base64 chart images (~87% of the
# notebook bytes here). That made "Jupyter Notebook" 78% of this repo
# while the actual source is Python and React.
#
# linguist-documentation keeps the notebooks fully visible and rendered on
# GitHub (they're part of the project's story) but leaves them out of the
# language statistics, so the bar reflects the code that was written.
*.ipynb linguist-documentation
